{"name":"Hillary","hex":"#a7a07e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Hillary","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A unisex given name from Latin.\nA female given name from Latin Hilaria.\n\nA male given name from Latin Hilarius, variant of Hilary.","A female given name from Latin Hilaria."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Hillary"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hilary (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Hilary, Hilarie or Hillary is a given name and surname, derived from the Latin hilarius meaning \"cheerful\", from hilaris, \"cheerful, merry\", which comes from the Greek ἱλαρός (hilaros), \"cheerful, merry\", which in turn comes from ἵλαος (hilaos), \"propitious, gracious\". Ilaria is the popular Italian feminine form, while Ilario is the Italian masculine one. Other male forms are Hilarion, Ilarion, and Illarion."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilary_(name)"},{"title":"Hillary Clinton","blocks":[{"text":"Hillary Diane Rodham Clinton is an American politician, lawyer and diplomat. She was the 67th United States secretary of state in the administration of Barack Obama from 2009 to 2013, a U.S. senator representing New York from 2001 to 2009, and the first lady of the United States from 1993 to 2001 as the wife of Bill Clinton. A member of the Democratic Party, she was the party's nominee in the 2016 presidential election, becoming the first woman to win a presidential nomination by a major U.S. political party. Clinton won the popular vote but lost the election to Republican Party nominee Donald Trump in the United States Electoral College. She is the only first lady of the United States to have run for, or held, elected office."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Former_United_States_Secretary_of_State_Hillary_Rodham_Clinton_at_the_U.S._Department_of_State_on_September_26%2C_2023_in_Washington%2C_D.C._14_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Former_United_States_Secretary_of_State_Hillary_Rodham_Clinton_at_the_U.S._Department_of_State_on_September_26%2C_2023_in_Washington%2C_D.C._14_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hillary_Clinton"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Hillary_Clinton_Portrait_%283x4_close_cropped%29.jpg/500px-Hillary_Clinton_Portrait_%283x4_close_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Hillary_Clinton_Portrait_%283x4_close_cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Hillary_Clinton_Portrait_%283x4_close_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Hillary_Clinton_Portrait_%283x4_close_cropped%29.jpg/500px-Hillary_Clinton_Portrait_%283x4_close_cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHillary_Clinton_Portrait_(3x4_close_cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Hillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg/500px-Hillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Hillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg/1280px-Hillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Hillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg/500px-Hillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rodham in Maine South High School's 1965 yearbook","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHillary_Clinton_in_1965_Eyrie.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/1968_Wellesley_College_Government_Presidential_Candidates_at_Panel.jpg/50